        <p>Planet: ♄ Shani (Saturn)</p>
        <p>Governs: Discipline, endurance, structure, patience, and long-term grounding</p>
        <p>Star Sapphire carries Saturn’s qualities, similar to Blue Sapphire, but expresses them differently. Where Blue Sapphire can feel direct and intense, Star Sapphire works through steadiness and alignment.</p>
        <p>The star within the gemstone is not decorative — it is symbolic. It represents a fixed point of clarity in movement, a centre that remains stable even when life feels uncertain.</p>
        <p>Star Sapphire is worn when life feels delayed, blocked, or structurally unstable — when the need is not speed, but direction. It supports patience, grounded thinking, and the ability to move forward with composure rather than urgency.</p>
        <p>It may be considered during Shani Mahadasha or Antardasha, or when endurance and mental stillness become essential.</p>
        <ul>
        <li>️ As with all Saturn gemstones, proper astrological guidance is strongly recommended.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>What Makes Star Sapphire Extraordinary</p>
        <p>Star Sapphire is defined by asterism — a natural six-rayed star formed by aligned rutile inclusions inside the stone.</p>
        <p>Unlike surface effects, this star is internal and permanent.</p>
        <ul>
        <li>The star moves smoothly as light moves</li>
        <li>Each stone has a unique star pattern</li>
        <li>The phenomenon cannot be artificially replicated with authenticity</li>
        </ul>
        <p>A real star moves. A fake one stays fixed.</p>
